{
  "_comment": "Server-side agent personas (design §WS3). Keypairs live outside the repo at keypairPath. Proposer and supporter roles share the same controller, checkpoint and activity system. A proposer proposes binding owners' agreements on parcels its wallet owns alone in the lens member's devnet owner registry (consensus.lens_devnet_owner; scripts/seed-lens-owners.mjs or agents/run.mjs --seed-owners registers them): every owner approves (unanimous) through receipts the lens member the runner operates verifies (the lens-member persona whose service names an operatorTokenEnv, lifecycle-01). On its next run the proposer approves as the owner, has that member attest the decision, records it on chain and executes. Its `agreement` block sets each agreement: `deadlineDays` after it is built (unexecuted by then, it expires), and `lamports` of escrow it funds at mint and execution requires (paid back to it at execution, refunded at expiry; 0 for none); `stakeUsdc` is its YES stake on that agreement's market. A lens-member persona runs the reference lens member (backend/lens/) via agents/lens-member-run.mjs; wallet null = key not generated yet. Society roles (contrarian, speculator) run through agents/society-run.mjs with a pure policy module at agents/policies/<role>.js; their `policy` block holds that module's parameters.",
